WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.932
Constrain the rewrite task.

00:00:01.932 --> 00:00:10.532
A good rewrite prompt can be very short: rewrite the user question as one concise search query for company policy

00:00:10.532 --> 00:00:12.602
documents. Preserve the original meaning.

00:00:12.602 --> 00:00:14.517
Do not answer the question.

00:00:14.517 --> 00:00:17.481
Do not invent dates or policy details.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:23.097
Why be so specific? Because the rewrite step has one job.

00:00:23.097 --> 00:00:25.597
It is not a general reasoning step.

00:00:25.597 --> 00:00:28.377
It should produce better search language.

00:00:28.377 --> 00:00:36.192
If you ask the model to explain, summarize, and search all at once, the output becomes harder to validate and may

00:00:36.192 --> 00:00:39.096
include facts that were never retrieved.

00:00:39.753 --> 00:00:46.120
For your project, define the output shape of each model call as narrowly as possible.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:49.270
A query rewriter should return a query.

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:51.620
A router should return a route.

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:54.140
A grader should return a grade.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:56.692
This keeps the workflow modular.
